<log-notes>
First log from
- start a meeting, clicked on notiifcation to start recording
- play system audio, discovered that the audio playback was not clear and sounded muble while recording/meeting was going on, why is this impacting audio playback?
- When i inspected the recorded audio and play it back, discovered that system audio is mumbly and crackles also. Wondering if recording the system audi to a separate file is better appraoch cause it seems like our current implementation for capturing system audio is not properly delivering the audio and also? Splitting the audio presents challenges with transcription but if we're not able to find the bug and this might be an optimal solution, present a design for us to discuss before implementing it.  
- I also discovered that the menubar icon for the app is still not showing during and after a meeting+transcription, is this a bug also visible in the log files
- Also after transscription is done and no other transcription items queued, the memeory usage still remains as 500mb+ so not sure the whisper model gets unloaded. Make sure we're unloading it in all idle state and when nothing to transcribe.
-See the logs for what i captured below for this session. Be smart and use tools and correct heuristics to scan through the logs since thats a lot of log lines. Note the log line for this ends before the next opening `<log-notes>` tag except if it end of file
</log-notes>
